# ============================================================================
# KπX global git excludes — secrets & universally-ignored artifacts
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Source of truth : $HOME/.agents/skills/k-git/assets/git-ignore-global
# Deployed as     : $HOME/.config/git/ignore (symlink)
#                   (git's default XDG excludesFile — auto-honored by ALL git
#                    repos without any config change)
#
# WHY: Loom discovers files in git repos via `git ls-files -co
# --exclude-standard`, which honors THIS file. Keeping real secrets and
# generated junk out of here keeps them out of every Loom index AND out of
# `git status` everywhere.
#
# ⚠️ CAVEAT: tracked files are still listed by `git ls-files -c` even when
# ignored. A `.env` COMMITTED to a repo stays visible to git AND Loom — fix
# at the source (untrack it) or add it to that repo's `.loomignore`.
# Non-git directories do NOT honor this file.
#
# ORDERING: 1. Secrets  ·  2. OS junk  ·  3. Editors/IDE  ·  4. Logs/temp
#           5. Python   ·  6. Node/JS   ·  7. JVM          ·  8. C/C++/Go/Rust
#           9. Test reports & coverage  ·  10. KπX agent/local-only docs
# ============================================================================


